      {"id":"lmc-note","type":"comment","position":{"x":-620,"y":-100},"data":{"text":"# Linear and Curve Mode Connectivity: same initialization, different training seed\n\nThis `small` template trains two CIFAR-10 classifiers from the identical ResNet initialization (`seed=0`) on the same full training set (`subsetSeed=0`). The only changed variable is the trainer RNG: endpoint A uses `trainSeed=0`; endpoint B uses `trainSeed=1`.\n\n**Default study budget:** 50,000 train images, 10,000 test images, batch size 128, and 50,000 updates per endpoint. Save the two endpoint checkpoints, run the 21-point linear interpolation barrier, then run the quadratic Bezier evaluator. The linear panel shows direct interpolation. The Bezier panel shows only the optimized curve and reports the linear-to-Bezier barrier comparison. BN calibration defaults to 100 train batches for both evaluators."},"style":{"width":760},"parentId":null,"extent":null,"hidden":null},
